
                    Dark sky, white ground, 
                    Famished eyes all around.

                    Ski the fields, fast as wind, 
                    The pack chases through the glen.

                    In the wood, now in front,
                    Salivating from the hunt.

                    Rigid bodies, snarling fangs,
                    Suddenly, haunches sprang.

                    Flailing poles, naked throat,
                    Running, gaping, crimson moat...



    You awake with a start. The tour bus was snaking its way through 
a long shadowed pass, the countryside below was covered in a snowflake 
blanket, and the only protrudence was the savage range of Styrian 
mountains. 

